@tradition name-on-the-beam
// Name on the beam (0.60.7, the traditions engineer, plans/plan-0607.html "Traditions"): after your first full shift
// the Works crew gather under the Works bay's cross beam and you paint your name beside everyone who's served there.
// Zeke hands you the pen. Your first Monday (day 1), straight from shift: the crew come as they clock off (after-shift).
// The beam and your name on it are the deck architect's (claude/deck-0607 "Places for 0.60.7": places 5-beam-1..8
// tagged name-beam, trace nameYours, a lasting mark from the day you join). The Works bay's crowd spots (venue) first,
// so the whole crew fits; it ends at 17:40 so they all walk to dinner together inside the shift-change rush (food_check's
// queue, 0.34.54). Zeke hosts (he hands you the pen): Calder works on to about 17:15 some Mondays and would miss it.
k: 441
title: Name on the beam
when: arrival monday
at: 17:05-17:40
min: 15
prio: 2
after-shift: yes
venue: works-bay
where: 5 pool @name-beam
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
hold: none
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, pell 95%, works 80%
anim: talk
host: torres-zeke
from: calder
trace: nameYours


== mail
- After shift tomorrow, stay in the bay a minute. There's a beam with a lot of names on it, and room for one more.

== ask
- Stay after shift. The beam's waiting for your name.
- Don't run off at five. Works has a thing. You'll like it.

== here
- There's mine. Wobbly letters. I was nervous.   #funny
- Every name up there fixed something on this ship.
- Go on. Big letters. Make it last.

== thanks
- Under the cross beam, the Works crew gather round. Zeke hands you the pen, and you add your name to all the others.   #warm

== chatter
- New hand's name goes on the beam tonight.
- I still look for my name on the beam, some days.   #warm
- Running out of beam, soon. Someone get a ladder.   #funny
